  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\ne V_0=h\\left(v-v_0\\right) & =h v-h v_0 \\\\\r\nV_0 & =\\left(\\frac{h}{e}\\right) v-\\left(\\frac{h}{e}\\right) v_0       \\quad \\quad \\ldots (i)\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\nFrom Eq. (i), it follows that the slope of the graph is $\\frac{h}{e}$. Therefore,\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\nh=e \\times \\text { slope } & =1.6 \\times 10^{-19} \\times \\frac{165-0}{(8-4) \\times 10^{15}} \\\\\r\n& =\\frac{1.6 \\times 10^{-19} \\times 16.5}{4 \\times 10^{15}}=6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{~J}-\\mathrm{s} .\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
